!--- 17. Ng acceleration ---
! [OPT] DO_NG enabled:
!   Ng acceleration was off, forcing pure Lambda/Newton iteration to
!   convergence.  For a model with ~10^4 depth-frequency unknowns Ng
!   acceleration typically cuts iteration count by 30-50%.
! [OPT] IBEG_NG reduced 20->10:
!   Starting Ng earlier (after the solution is past the wildly oscillatory
!   phase but before the slow linear convergence sets in) is more efficient.
! [OPT] BW_NG reduced 60->30:
!   A narrower Ng bandwidth is more stable for models where the solution
!   changes character across the shock front; 30 depths is typically
!   sufficient to span the photospheric region.
! [OPT] ITS/NG reduced 8->4:
!   More frequent Ng steps (every 4 rather than every 8 iterations)
!   accelerates convergence without adding instability once IBEG_NG
!   has been passed.
T               [DO_NG]        ! [OPT] was F; enable Ng acceleration
5.0D0           [BEG_NG]       ! Max correction (%) to attempt Ng
10              [IBEG_NG]      ! [OPT] was 20; start Ng earlier
30              [BW_NG]        ! [OPT] was 60; narrower Ng block
4               [ITS/NG]       ! [OPT] was 8; more frequent Ng steps

